\section{Paper List Widget}
\label{sec:paper-list-widget}

The main interface displays papers in a navigable list. Each paper shows its
title, authors, year, and current review status using color coding.

\subsection{Widget Composition in Textual}

Textual uses a composition model where complex interfaces are built from
simple widgets. Our [[PaperListItem]] extends [[ListItem]] (a built-in widget)
and yields [[Static]] widgets containing formatted text.

The [[compose]] method is Textual's pattern for declarative UI: rather than
imperatively creating and adding widgets, we yield the widgets we want and
Textual handles layout and rendering.

\subsection{Visual Feedback Through Color}

Color coding provides immediate visual feedback about review progress:
\begin{description}
\item[Green checkmark (\texttt{✓})] Paper marked as kept
\item[Red cross (\texttt{✗})] Paper marked as discarded
\item[Dim circle (\texttt{○})] Paper still pending review
\item[Yellow notepad (\texttt{📝})] Paper has attached notes
\item[Magenta robot (\texttt{🤖}) or \texttt{A}] An unreviewed decision of
  an LLM or of an AI agent (\cref{sec:review-source}), with its
  confidence when one was recorded; cyan with a checkmark once a human
  has reviewed it
\end{description}
The agent gets a letter of its own because its decisions are a
different procedure from the classifier's, and a reviewer confirming a
batch should know whose proposals they are confirming.
A decision whose stored source Scholar does not know shows a magenta
question mark and is queued like the machine decisions; confirming it
makes it a human decision (\cref{sec:review-source}).
The confirmation messages name the machine too, so one helper says
which machine a source belongs to.

<<tui paper list widget>>=
def machine_name(source: ReviewSource) -> str:
    """Name the machine behind a decision source: "agent", "LLM",
    "unknown-source" or ""."""
    if source.is_unknown:
        return "unknown-source"
    if source in (ReviewSource.AGENT_UNREVIEWED, ReviewSource.AGENT_REVIEWED):
        return "agent"
    return "LLM" if source.is_machine else ""


@

In notes-only mode, we hide the status indicator since keep/discard
doesn't apply---the user is just browsing papers with notes.

