\paragraph{Testing the procedure.}
The tests drive the real application headless, through
[[TestBlindReview.run]] (\cref{sec:tui-blind-review}) without blind
mode, on a session that uses categories: an agent's keep under
[[supports-claim]] with a reason, a pending paper and a human's discard
with a reason in words.  They check the refused pair on both screens
(nothing stored, the notification, the screen kept), the refused
confirmation of a stored pair, a changed category as a change with the
prompt opening by itself and dismissed with Escape, a reason typed and
one picked from the earlier ones, the key on a pending paper, the
detail screen's lines, and a session without categories.  One-key
confirmation is pinned field by field: the decision differs from the
one before only in the fields a confirmation always set (the source and
the record of the review, with the reviewer's name that [[run]] gives).

