The TUI's enrichment records an adopted preprint as a rename too
(\cref{sec:session-renames} in the review chapter), so a sample drawn
before it still names the paper.  The enrichment is stood in for,
since it would ask the providers; the app, its thread and its screens
are real.

The enrichment runs in a plain thread, not a Textual worker, so the
test cannot wait for it through the app's workers.  It waits for the
last thing the thread does, the notification of what was enriched, and
then for the app to be idle ([[settle_after_enrichment]]).  A first
version left as soon as the rename was recorded, which happens inside
the same callback before the notification and before the detail screen
is recomposed; under load the app then shut down while the recompose
was still mounting a new header, whose title callback found no title
widget (Textual's [[NoMatches]] for [[HeaderTitle]]): 1 failure in 30
runs beside a full test run.

