Let's verify the helpers on decisions built in code.  The reviewer
made a confirmed decision of their name, and neither an unreviewed
machine decision nor another human's; a screening set aside by a reset
is not the reviewer's verdict any more; a paper drawn in the second
band of a banded draw names that band, and one reset after a first
draw and drawn again names the later sample, whose draw is the
decision it holds now.  The last test checks what the notice of blind
mode adds for a banded sample of discards ([[sample_giveaway]], in the
review module) and that it adds nothing for a sample of both statuses.

