\subsection{Blind mode in the application}

The application keeps three things for blind mode: [[blind]], whether
it is on, [[blind_unbroken]], whether it has been on since the TUI
started (below), and [[reviewer]], the name.  [[blind_state]] tells what blind
mode does with a decision: nothing ([[None]], blind mode off or a paper
the sample filter does not list), hide it, show it revealed (the
reviewer has screened it), or refuse it ([[own]], the reviewer made
it).  The list asks for every row, so it computes the sample's queue
once and passes it in; the detail screen asks for one paper.

<<app methods for blind review>>=
def blind_queue(self) -> set[int]:
    """The decisions blind mode concerns: those the sample filter lists."""
    if not self.blind:
        return set()
    from scholar.llm_review import sampled_for_review
    return {id(d) for d in sampled_for_review(self.session)}

def blind_state(self, decision: ReviewDecision,
                queue: set[int] | None = None) -> str | None:
    """None, "hidden", "revealed" or "own": what blind mode does with
    `decision` (`queue` from `blind_queue`, computed if not given)."""
    if not self.blind:
        return None
    if id(decision) not in (self.blind_queue() if queue is None else queue):
        return None
    if made_by_reviewer(decision, self.reviewer):
        return "own"
    if reviewer_screening(decision, self.reviewer) is not None:
        return "revealed"
    return "hidden"
@

Blind mode starts in one of two ways, and the difference is what
[[blind_unbroken]] keeps.  Started with the TUI ([[--blind]], the
[[blind]] argument of the application), it is switched on in
[[on_mount]] before the list is first drawn, so no verdict of the
sample has been on the screen; [[blind_unbroken]] is then true, and
stays true until blind mode is switched off.  Switched on with [[b]]
during a run, it hides from then on, but the list was drawn before with
its marks, so [[blind_unbroken]] is false and stays false for the run.
Either way it needs review mode (notes mode decides nothing), a sample
and a name, asked for when [[--by]] gave none; without one it stays
off.  [[b]] is taken only in the paper list: a detail screen or a
dialog on top was drawn as it was, and switching blind mode under it
would claim a blindness that screen does not have.

<<app methods for blind review>>=
def _start_blind_at_mount(self) -> None:
    """Start blind mode before the list is drawn, if asked to."""
    if not self.blind_requested:
        return
    if not self.review_mode or not self.session.llm_samples:
        self.notify("No review sample in this session; blind mode is "
                    "off. Draw one with `scholar llm sample`.",
                    severity="warning", markup=False)
        return
    self.blind = True
    self.blind_unbroken = True
    self.current_filter = "llm_sample"
    if self.reviewer is None:
        self.push_screen(ReviewerNameModal(), self._on_reviewer_named)
    else:
        self._notify_blind()

def action_toggle_blind(self) -> None:
    """Switch blind review of the sample on or off."""
    if not self.review_mode:
        self.notify("Blind review is for review mode", severity="warning")
        return
    if len(self.screen_stack) > 1:
        self.notify("Switch blind mode in the paper list: this screen was "
                    "drawn as it is", severity="warning")
        return
    if self.blind:
        self.blind = False
        self.blind_unbroken = False
        self.notify("Blind mode off")
        self._refresh_list()
        self._update_status()
        return
    if not self.session.llm_samples:
        self.notify("No review sample in this session; draw one with "
                    "`scholar llm sample`", severity="warning",
                    markup=False)
        return
    self.blind = True
    self.blind_unbroken = False
    self.current_filter = "llm_sample"
    self.current_index = 0
    if self.reviewer is None:
        self.push_screen(ReviewerNameModal(), self._on_reviewer_named)
    else:
        self._notify_blind()
    self._refresh_list()
    self._update_status()

def _on_reviewer_named(self, name: str | None) -> None:
    """Keep blind mode on under the name given; off without one."""
    if name:
        self.reviewer = name
        self._notify_blind()
    else:
        self.blind = False
        self.blind_unbroken = False
        self.notify("Blind mode needs your name; it is off",
                    severity="warning")
    self._refresh_list()
    self._update_status()

def _notify_blind(self) -> None:
    """Say what blind mode hides, and what the samples tell anyway."""
    from scholar.llm_review import sampled_for_review

    giveaway = sample_giveaway(self.session,
                               sampled_for_review(self.session))
    self.notify(BLIND_MODE_NOTICE + (f"\n{giveaway}" if giveaway else ""),
                markup=False, timeout=15)

def blind_status_text(self) -> str:
    """The status bar's blind mode indicator, "" when off."""
    if not self.blind:
        return ""
    label = "Blind" if self.blind_unbroken \
        else "Blind (verdicts were shown earlier in this run)"
    return (f" | [bold blue]{label}: {escape(self.reviewer or '')}"
            "[/bold blue]")
