\subsection{Testing blind mode}

The tests drive the real application headless, as those of the sample
filter do (\cref{FilterModal}).  The session has one sampled paper, an
LLM's discard with confidence, tags and a reason; one unsampled LLM
keep; and a human's keep.  [[run]] starts the application in blind mode
unless told otherwise, presses the keys and calls [[inspect]] on the
running application; the notifications are kept in [[notices]].
[[text]] collects what the current screen shows, and [[offered]] the
tags a tag dialog offers, so that a test can check what is and is not
there.

